{"article_ids": ["ea2f0f9df4e1cd12"], "canonical_title": "Formally verifying agent-written full-stack web apps with PDD Kit", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.96, "description": "Microsoft Research announced PDD Kit, a tool that turns developer intent into Verus formal specifications, then automatically proves that code generated by AI agents satisfies those specifications for all inputs. Where full proofs are infeasible, the kit falls back to conventional testing. This approach lets developers verify full‑stack web applications created by AI without reviewing each line of code.", "entities": ["term:pdd"], "first_seen": "2026-11-05T16:00:00Z", "id": "evt_ea2f0f9df4e1cd12", "importance_score": 6.45, "last_updated": "2026-11-05T16:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["microsoft-research"]}
{"article_ids": ["ff40942fae52f001"], "canonical_title": "FlashOffloading: Low-Latency KV Cache Offloading for Long-Context LLM Serving", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.73, "description": "The paper introduces FlashOffloading, a technique that moves the key‑value cache used by large language model inference from high‑bandwidth memory (HBM) to host DRAM. This frees HBM capacity, allowing higher concurrency for long‑context queries, while addressing the latency increase caused by host‑to‑device transfers and cache management overhead.", "entities": ["term:dram", "term:hbm", "term:kv"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_ff40942fae52f001", "importance_score": 6.29, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["cb9b318f703a0f1a"], "canonical_title": "Vera Delivers the Best of Both Worlds: Highest Throughput and Fastest Agents", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.6, "description": "Nvidia announced its Vera platform, which it says delivers the highest throughput and fastest AI agents by improving the CPU side of the workload. The announcement notes that AI agents perform tasks such as searching, querying databases, writing and testing code, and taking actions, and that each step relies on CPU execution while moving between GPU reasoning and CPU execution.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-11-05T20:00:41Z", "id": "evt_cb9b318f703a0f1a", "importance_score": 6.048, "last_updated": "2026-11-05T20:00:41Z", "source_ids": ["nvidia"]}
{"article_ids": ["4c861a74d24931e0"], "canonical_title": "Synthesizing symbolic models of human and machine reasoning at scale", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "Researchers introduced Behavior-Conditioned Symbolic Synthesis (BCSS), an automated search technique that generates deterministic, interpretable symbolic programs. The approach leverages recent AI advances to reduce the need for manual engineering and to handle larger, more complex symbolic models than previously feasible.", "entities": ["term:bc"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_4c861a74d24931e0", "importance_score": 5.84, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["418006ee56680f7c"], "canonical_title": "Goal-Branching LaCAM: Temporary Goals as Search Branches in Dense Multi-Agent Pathfinding", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "LaCAM is a depth‑first search based solver for multi‑agent pathfinding that uses PIBT to generate successors and lazily adds single‑agent constraints. The paper introduces Goal‑Branching LaCAM, which treats temporary goals as separate search branches to better explore alternatives when dense, corridor‑heavy instances cause deadlocks that require coordinated moves of several agents away from their goals.", "entities": ["term:mapf", "term:pibt"], "first_seen": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_418006ee56680f7c", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-11-06T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
